{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "תועה", :translit "to'eh", :gloss "straying"} {:he "חמורו תועה", :translit "chamoro to'eh", :gloss "his donkey straying"} {:he "והנה תועה בשדה", :translit "vehineh to'eh basadeh", :gloss "and behold straying in the field"} {:he "אדם תועה מדרך השכל", :translit "adam to'eh miderech ha-sechel", :gloss "a man straying from the way of reason"} {:he "מצא פרה רועה אין זו אבידה", :translit "matzah parah ro'ah ein zu aveidah", :gloss "one found a cow grazing — this is not lost property"} {:he "מצא חמור וכליו הפוכים הרי זו אבידה", :translit "matzah chamor uchelav hofchim harei zu aveidah", :gloss "one found a donkey with its gear inverted — this is lost property"} {:he "חמורו תועה", :translit "chamoro to'eh", :gloss "his donkey straying"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["חמורו תועה" "והנה תועה בשדה" "אדם תועה מדרך השכל"]}], :frame {:text "The Talmud distinguishes between an animal found grazing normally, which is presumed to be wandering and not yet lost, and one found with its gear inverted, which is considered lost property. A donkey whose saddle-bags are turned upside down demonstrates that it slipped off the road, establishing it as lost property (Bava Metzia 31a). Ba'al HaTurim cites this criterion to explain why the verse specifies חמורו תועה — the donkey is straying in a field, having departed from the road.", :sources ["Bava Metzia 31a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["חמורו תועה" "והנה תועה בשדה" "אדם תועה מדרך השכל"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "חמורו תועה", :refs ["Exodus 23:4"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "והנה תועה בשדה", :refs ["Genesis 37:15"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "אדם תועה מדרך השכל", :refs ["Proverbs 21:16"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:18:42.929653842Z", :model "glm-5.2"}